{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Jacob.</b> Wherever 'these' (אלה) is said, it disqualifies the preceding ones, to say: the former were wicked, sons of bastardy, and these are righteous, from a fit drop, and they are the sons of Judah and Joseph, who are mentioned further on in the passage." "<b>These are the generations of Jacob: Joseph.</b> After the matter was interrupted with the matter of Joseph and it began with another matter, when it returned to its original matter it said, 'These are the generations of Jacob: Joseph.' And so we find with Noah." "<b>He was shepherding his brothers.</b> According to the way of the world, Scripture calls the sons of Leah 'his brothers,' and not the sons of the handmaids. Another interpretation: <b>And he was a youth</b> — that is, while he was still a youth he would shepherd his brothers, and there is no disgrace for the son of the mistress, while still a youth, to pasture his father's flocks with the sons of the handmaids. And the verse is inverted: 'and he, a youth, was shepherding with the flock, his brothers, the sons of Bilhah and the sons of Zilpah.' And do not wonder that he would bring their evil report to their father, for he was a youth." "<b>With the flock.</b> It does not say 'the flock' (הצאן), for he would watch over them — watch what they do — and 'with the flock,' that they would not cause damage, for he was trustworthy to his father." "<b>And Joseph brought their evil report.</b> Therefore they all hated him, as it is said, 'and they hated him' — that is, all the sons of the handmaids, because of the report; and the sons of the mistress were jealous of him, because their father loved him more than all his brothers, and they feared lest Jacob make him ruler over them, just as Isaac wanted to say to Esau, 'be lord over your brothers,' because he loved him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:40.929097613Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}